WEBVTT

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.870
<i>Even I...</i>

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:12.250
Second!

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:15.710
Safe!

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.090
Safe!

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.740
All right!

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.050
Great job, Miyazaki!

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.220
All right! A double play!

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.880
Run five!

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.350
We aren't very lucky, are we?

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.270
No, luck won't come to those who have thrown all hope away.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.740
They've called luck to themselves.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:49.240
But the ones to laugh last will be our team.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.680
All right!

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.730
It's 8-5!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.680
We're not gonna stop!

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.140
Keep going, Yamamoto!

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.100
Out!

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.520
Batting eighth: right fielder, Noguchi-kun.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.230
Strike! Out!

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.700
Three outs, change!

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:51.630
I-I'm sorry...

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.150
I-I'm sorry...

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.160
Don't mind, don't mind.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.340
There're still two innings left, and it's only a three run difference.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.770
We can win!

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.870
As long as they don't get any more runs, that is.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.330
What?

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.700
If you put me on the bench for the rest of these two innings,

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.550
who's going to be the pitcher?

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.720
Isn't it obvious?

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.700
There's only me.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.010
Are you serious?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.690
When you were coming back from home you were limping.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.650
In your condition, to put all your weight on your right leg when you plant,

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:29.580
can you pitch properly, senpai?

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.970
You...

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:34.370
Is it fun for you to predict everything that happens in life before it happens?

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.630
It's not whether I can or can't do it.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.540
If you're a man, it's only whether you do it or not.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.880
And if it's something you like, then even more so.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:55.010
Seishuu High School pitching change: replacing Shimizu-kun is Shigeno-kun.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.980
It's the number 10 from earlier.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.640
That looks pretty fast.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.180
<i>He's better at pitching than batting, huh?</i>

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.610
<i>It seems as though he's been hurt,
so they left him in reserve until now.</i>

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.390
Don't force yourself, Shigeno.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:17.600
Yeah, if it's too hard for you, let them hit it.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.550
We'll protect you.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.820
Idiot! That doesn't have any persuasive power at all... 

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.610
Coming from you, who made three errors.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:25.830
What'd you say!?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.350
Well, I'll just take it easy. 

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.550
They're not an opponent to go all-out on.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:36.030
Batting third: left fielder, Asaoka-kun.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.350
Play!

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.000
<i>Three-run difference, huh?</i>

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.270
<i>They should be feeling the pressure from our team's spirit for sure.</i>

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.650
<i>To make them panic more,</i>

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.320
<i>and in order to give our players more courage and confidence,</i>

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.780
<i>I can't hold back!</i>

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:09.870
S-Strike!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.050
S-Strike!

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.890
"Take it easy"?

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:16.720
You bastard...

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.840
Did you see that!?

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.430
Yeah, who <i>is</i> that pitcher?

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.050
<i>I see...</i>

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.400
<i>At least your pitch's speed has evolved, Honda-kun.</i>

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.320
Strike! Batter out!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.390
Three outs, change!

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.480
Amazing, amazing!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.450
Three batters and three strikeouts.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.360
There's nothing wrong with your leg!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.210
Couldn't you have been the starting pitcher?

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.940
Idiot.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:55.030
If I was the starting pitcher against such an opponent, it wouldn't be practice, right?

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:57.900
That's why I've been reserving myself up till now.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.630
You've been reserving too much!

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.370
All right! Let's make our comeback at this tempo!

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:06.140
The game is completely in our favor!

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.150
Hey, Honda, where're you going?

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.640
You're the next batter!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.870
Yeah. Sorry, I've got to go to the bathroom.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.120
Please tell Takahashi to stall.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.750
Ball.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:27.040
Good job, good job! Keep watching the ball!

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:35.050
This is bad. 

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:40.010
At the worst, I thought that 30 pitches or so would be easy.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:46.120
But I guess going all-out just now was a mistake.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:50.560
Weren't you going to the bathroom?

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.090
The bench is hot and all.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:58.210
So I thought I'd take a rest where it's cooler...

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.860
Is it that bad?

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.370
Don't worry.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:07.290
I know it's useless to try and stop you.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.860
But you know what?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.920
The way you are now, are you going to be able to get to where you want to go?

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.260
You're really meddlesome.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:18.880
Shigeno!

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:26.330
To tell you the truth, we have our hands full trying not to get in your way. 

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:31.480
Without you, we're not at the level where we're able to continue winning till the game against Kaido.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:33.440
But you know...

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:36.580
Stop trying to act cool all by yourself!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:41.090
If it's tough for you, you can show your weakness to us!

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.370
If I feel like it.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:52.730
Oh, he's here! He's here!

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:53.420
He's here!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.020
Hey, what're you doing, Shigeno?

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.380
I'm sorry. I'm very sorry. {(keeps going)}

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.380
Takahashi got four balls and is on base!

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:00.380
My bad, my bad.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.970
All right!

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.550
Let's change the game this inning!

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.020
Batting first: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:15.490
Play!

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.880
<i>Damn it. </i>

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.650
<i>With this leg, I won't be able to run very fast.</i>

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:25.160
<i>But there's one way I won't have to run.</i>

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:28.280
<i>And that's... to hit a home run!</i>

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.500
Pitcher!

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.000
<i>Damn! This is the worst!</i>

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:43.650
Safe! Safe!

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:44.630
Safe! Safe!

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.820
All right!

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.850
No outs, and runners on first and second!

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:52.270
<i>It hurts!</i>

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.230
<i>But I can't do this.</i>

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.190
<i>Stand up!</i>

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:00.190
<i>Stand up right now!</i>

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.500
<i>If I show my weakness right here,</i>

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:07.880
<i>won't I dampen the team's "comeback" mood?</i>

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.770
<i>This doesn't hurt at all!</i>

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:12.780
<i>Stand up!</i>

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.460
<i>Stand up and laugh, Shigeno Goro!</i>

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.360
What the heck?

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.380
Was he the kind of guy who would get so happy about an infield hit?

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.250
But that's to be expected of Shigeno-senpai!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.830
What amazing fighting spirit!

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.100
Darling's the best!

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:36.100
<i>That idiot!</i>

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.080
Dead ball.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.660
That didn't hurt at all!

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.120
All right! Bases loaded!

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.870
Batting third: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:56.830
<i>We'll win!</i>

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.930
<i>Let's win for sure, Shigeno!</i>

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:02.750
<i>Your leg's already at its limit.</i>

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:05.760
<i>In order to not put anymore pressure on it,</i>

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.430
<i>I have to hit it past the outfield!</i>

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:20.060
G-Go over!

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:24.940
A comeback...

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.320
grand slam...

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:31.780
All right!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.670
Nice, Tashiro!

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.240
You did it!

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.200
No way...

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.170
All right!

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:45.960
We did it!

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.140
Here, Komori.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.600
Oh, thanks, Yamane-kun.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:10:59.730
But...

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:01.560
they're playing an exciting game, aren't they?

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.360
Any team that Honda's on...

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.220
naturally ends up like this, huh?

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.220
Yeah.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:12.300
But that last batter played on the Honmoku Seniors and was a strong clean-up hitter.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.990
It isn't surprising that he hit the ball with a pitcher of that level.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:17.910
Out!

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.480
That's just like you.

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:22.170
You've... already researched all that?

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:27.680
Yeah. After all, they might be our next opponent.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:30.090
Well, whichever team wins,

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.180
I already have plenty of strategies to beat them.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:37.640
But if I had to pick one of them, Seishuu would be better for us.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.100
Strike! Batter out!

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.930
Three outs, change!

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:45.370
All right!

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.690
Let's make sure they don't score any runs this inning, win, and drink some sake!

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:49.370
All right!

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.030
Don't drink!

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.030
Let's drink!

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:57.150
Don't be so depressed.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.200
They only have a one-run lead.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.590
B-But Coach...

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:05.140
I don't think we'll be able to get runs that easily off of that pitcher!

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.880
It's possible.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.600
With that pitcher now, one run...

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:14.640
No, getting two runs wouldn't be that hard.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:18.100
It's too early to give up.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.560
Shigeno.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:21.510
Huh?

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.560
No, never mind.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:28.980
Let's win!

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:31.750
Yeah.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:37.450
This is a free fansub.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:37.450
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:38.910
Play!

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.100
<i>You don't have to swing at all.</i>

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.380
<i>If my eyes don't deceive me... he's already...</i>

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.530
<i>useless.</i>

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:52.430
Ball!

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:01.180
Ball!

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:08.360
<i>Sorry, kid. I'm sorry to say, but I'll have you see Hell.</i>

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.410
<i>The last inning after our comeback... </i>

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:16.820
<i>Just three outs left.</i>

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:21.790
<i>But the real trial begins now, Nogoro-kun.</i>

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.410
Ball. 

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.480
Four balls.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:27.020
All right!

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:28.130
We've got a runner on base!

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:30.290
<i>Damn!</i>

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.360
<i>Because I can't put too much weight on my right leg,</i>

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.300
<i>my form is off, and my pitches are getting hit.</i>

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:38.760
Shigeno.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.180
<i>Do your best, Shigeno.</i>

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.060
<i>If we lose, it'll all be in vain.</i>

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:54.780
Ball!

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:03.060
<i>It's a disappointment, but based on your leg's condition,</i>

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:06.710
<i>you won't be able to throw pitches or field anymore.</i>

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:08.920
Ball.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:10.670
Ball.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:13.490
<i>With only ten members, on a newly formed baseball team,</i>

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:17.170
<i>I'll give you credit for surviving this long.</i>

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:24.640
<i>But it's still too early for you to think of winning the Kanagawa Tournament and leaving your name in its history.</i>

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:27.220
Ball.

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:28.560
Four balls.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.400
T-Time!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.520
T-Time!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:34.250
What the...?

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.150
Is there something wrong with Honda?

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:40.540
It seems as though he's hurt his leg.

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:45.160
With the way he is now, he probably won't be able to play in the game against us.

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:46.770
Although...

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:50.120
It's becoming uncertain whether or not they can actually win this game.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:53.460
What?

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:55.800
Not "what."

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.290
I said it's okay even if they hit it...

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.000
Just try and get strikes first.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.690
You can't pitch well with that leg, can you?

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:05.970
If you're going to throw four balls and self-destruct, let them hit it and us catch it.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:12.300
You're asking me to trust you guys, who said you have your hands full trying not get in my way?

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.240
I was joking.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:21.660
At this rate, I'm the one who's in everyone's way.

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.580
Batting eighth: second baseman, Iwashita-kun.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:32.750
Strike!

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:33.880
All right.

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:40.780
<i>So they stopped throwing fastballs and came to get strikes, huh?</i>

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.680
<i>Well then... we'll have them take us home.</i>

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:50.900
To first!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:52.980
Out!

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:54.210
All right!

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.440
One out and one run to make a comeback!

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:00.360
S-Shigeno!

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:06.990
Two more. 

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:09.380
Just two more outs... Shigeno.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:12.570
Shigeno-senpai...

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.000
That guy... His condition's that bad?

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:18.730
You reap what you sow!

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:22.970
This happened because he didn't think about the consequences and put me on the bench.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:24.470
Taiga!

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:29.640
Batting ninth: catcher, Shinohara-kun.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:32.850
<i>One out with runners on second and third.</i>

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.750
<i>There's no mistake that there'll be a squeeze somewhere.</i>

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.320
<i>First base is open.</i>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:42.320
<i>We'll pretend to make it a battle and throw balls, Shigeno.</i>

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:45.310
Four balls.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.160
<i>Shoot! Did he see through it?</i>

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:53.120
You're inexperienced.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:57.080
Batting first: center fielder, Kubo-kun.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:58.560
<i>Damn.</i>

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:02.550
<i>This is bad. They're forcing us more and more into a corner.</i>

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:05.360
<i>This is my fault for using passive tactics. </i>

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:08.200
<i>If someone makes an error, a run will score easily.</i>

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.510
<i>Damn.</i>

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:12.390
<i>When are you going to come with a squeeze?</i>

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:14.550
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.050
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>When should I make him throw a ball?</i>

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:19.860
Tashiro!

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.340
I don't care.

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.890
It's an all-out battle! 

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:26.860
I'll pitch an extremely fast pitch that they won't be able to squeeze bunt right down the middle!

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:32.050
What? 

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:33.890
<i>That idiot!</i>

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:35.140
<i>What's he saying?</i>

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:38.960
<i>Doesn't he understand that he won't be able to get strikes anymore with those pitches?</i>

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:43.880
<i>Wait. Just observe for now.</i>

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.680
<i>Don't do it, Shigeno. They'll just score more runs on us!</i>

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.060
Strike!

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:54.060
W-What?

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:56.440
What part of that is a fastball?

00:17:56.440 --> 00:18:00.130
It's the same as before... a regular speed strike, right?

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.020
Yes...

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.480
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.500
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.270
<i>No. </i>

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.700
<i>It's too dangerous.</i>

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:10.660
<i>I can't give the sign for a squeeze.</i>

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:13.740
Strike!

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.700
All right! They're in trouble!

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:17.660
I see...

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:25.170
<i>H-He tricked me! That kid's yell was just a bluff.</i>

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:28.590
<i>To seal the squeeze and to build up the count,</i>

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:31.890
<i>he only pretended that he was going to throw a fast pitch that'd end up as a ball.</i>

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.600
<i>There's nothing we can do about it. Hit it!</i>

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:38.350
<i>With those pitches, it's possible to hit at least a sacrifice fly.</i>

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:44.110
<i>What!?</i>

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:46.110
Strike! Batter out!

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:47.610
All right!

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:48.820
He did it!

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:55.450
Y-You idiot! Didn't I tell you not to swing at those fast pitches?

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:56.790
I-I'm sorry...

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:01.490
<i>Corner him with slow pitches first,
and then make him swing when that fast pitch comes...</i>

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:03.790
<i>You do well in the clutch, Honda!</i>

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:06.530
C-Calm down, Sakakibara!

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:08.920
He doesn't have any more tricks up his sleeve.

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:12.160
Just try and hit the balls that are in the strike zone.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:13.260
O-Okay.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.220
Batting second: right fielder, Sakakibara-kun.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:21.190
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:25.320
<i>Because my leg hurts so badly, my vision's getting blurry. </i>

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.610
<i>My leg's all worn-out...</i>

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.830
<i>My serious fastballs don't work...</i>

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:38.540
<i>I don't have any way to strike this guy out for sure.</i>

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:40.480
<i>Damn!</i>

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.770
Do your best, Shigeno!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.500
Just one more person!

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.960
We'll definitely stop him for you!

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:52.890
Come on! Shigeno!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:21.790
A-All right!

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.750
A-All right!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.710
Out! Game over!

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:29.710
We did it!

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:29.710
Shigeno!

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:30.810
Nice game.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:32.780
We won! We won!

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:35.790
<i>Nice game.</i>

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.890
<i>However... </i>

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:40.890
<i>we might have paid too high a price for this victory.</i>

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.150
No, Coach...

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.910
It wasn't Youka.

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:49.320
It was 9-8; Seishuu won.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:51.930
Yes.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.850
I have a video, so please watch it later.

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:57.150
Well then, I'll see you later.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:58.840
Video?

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:00.670
Where did you have such a thing?

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:03.160
Komori!

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.310
I had Oobayashi-kun film it for me.

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:11.030
If it's from the side of the back screen,
you can figure out the batter's weak points better.

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:13.130
It was an amazing game, wasn't it?

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:15.680
I forgot that they are going up against us next,

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:18.600
and started cheering for Honda-kun's team without noticing it.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:20.390
Did you film it correctly?

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:21.810
Yeah. It's perfect.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:22.590
Are you sure?

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:23.330
It wasn't shaking or anything?

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.260
No, it wasn't shaking.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:26.020
<i>Sorry, Honda.</i>

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:29.320
<i>To tell you the truth, after watching this game,</i>

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:32.210
<i>I don't feel threatened by your team at all.</i>

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:37.570
<i>At that level, it's not that easy for you to be able to get somewhere in Kanagawa. </i>

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.410
Hey! What're you doing!?

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:42.550
Let me go!

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:44.470
Ow! You...

00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:45.390
Hey! Nakamura!

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:46.250
Help get it off of him!

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:48.780
Eh? What are you saying?

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:51.210
How can you ask a lady to do such a thing?

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.250
Idiot! Not his pants!

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:54.170
His socks!

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.630
Shigeno!

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:03.600
How horrible...

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:04.960
Shut up!

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.670
I'm not on display!

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:08.940
If you put spit on this kind of injury, it'll get better!

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:11.350
When's the Mifune game?

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:12.940
Two days after tomorrow.

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:13.940
Three days.

00:22:15.150 --> 00:22:17.000
Three days is plenty!

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:20.560
Like I could leave it up to Taiga, who has no passion.

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:22.660
Oh, is that so?

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:24.450
I understand.

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:27.850
I won't ever be the pitcher again.

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:29.350
Stop joking around.

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:33.340
Just whose fault do you think it is that a junior had to get up on the mound?

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:36.340
Even if you beg me to, I won't do it!

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:41.050
H-Hey, wait a minute, Taiga!

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:42.390
Sister! Stop him!

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.850
She went home a long time ago.

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:47.570
Nogoro-kun.

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:52.390
I'm thankful that you tried your hardest in today's game.

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:57.320
However, I cannot pretend that you aren't hurt with the condition you are in right now.

00:22:59.050 --> 00:23:03.400
We can only go and get a doctor's diagnosis, then take the necessary actions.

00:24:40.920 --> 00:24:44.890
Our second opponent is Mifune High School, which is led by my former catcher, Komori.

00:24:44.890 --> 00:24:48.310
Even if they're my friends, I can't allow them to win!

00:24:48.310 --> 00:24:51.310
But, before that, I have to do something about this leg.

00:24:52.510 --> 00:24:54.020
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.020 --> 00:24:55.020
The Mifune Game Begins!

00:24:55.500 --> 00:24:57.770
Run to the stage of your dreams!
